# Humpback whale song: segmentation and unit-similarity (ELEC5305)

Reproduce and evaluate established signal-processing methods for automatic segmentation of humpback whale
song units, and test whether acoustic similarity measures reveal repeated unit types.

## Layout
- `matlab/` : the project code (run from this folder)
  - `params.m` all parameters
  - `load_song.m`, `preprocess_song.m` read, resample to 8 kHz, band-pass 80-3500 Hz
  - `band_envelope_db.m`, `detect_units.m` single / double-threshold energy detectors
  - `evaluate_segmentation.m` IoU matching -> missed, false, precision/recall/F1, onset/offset error
  - `mel_filterbank.m`, `mfcc_frames.m`, `unit_representations.m` four unit descriptors
  - `cluster_units.m`, `adjusted_rand.m` hierarchical clustering + agreement with true unit type
  - `run_baseline.m`, `run_snr_comparison.m` synthetic-data experiments
  - `run_real_data.m` template for NIPS4B / Watkins recordings
- `python/` : mirror of the pipeline with identical parameters, used to generate the first results
  (`python3 run_experiments.py`)
- `results/` : figures, synthetic test songs + ground truth, run log

## Requirements
MATLAB with Signal Processing Toolbox and Statistics and Machine Learning Toolbox.
The whale audio is too big to upload to matlaab.but can be found online.

## Status
Synthetic-data validation only. The double-threshold detector is a re-implementation from the published
description (Pace et al., 2010), not Pace's original code. Next: real recording, hand annotation of 30-50 units.
